# TN Title: Part V Flow on Title → Survey-Wise Matrix + Flow Chart

## Context
CMS IndusLaw / advocate Title Scrutiny Reports (TSR) for Tamil Nadu properties contain a Part V "Flow on Title" section — the definitive chain of ownership from original pattadar to current owner. This reference covers extracting that data into a structured Google Sheets matrix WITH flow charts.

## Workflow

### 1. Extract TSR Text
```bash
pdftotext -layout path/to/tsr.pdf /tmp/tsr_output.txt
```
Read the output with `read_file` — Part V starts at "PART-V" / "FLOW ON TITLE".

### 2. Identify Survey Series
Group by survey series (158, 166, 167, 168, 176, 177). Each series has sub-numbers (1A1A, 1B2, 1C3, etc.) with bifurcations from parent surveys.

### 3. Build Family Groups (PART_V_FlowOnTitle)
Group surveys by family. Each family section = one title flow (e.g., Lakshmana Reddy family covers 158/1A1A, 158/1A1B, 167/1A, 168/1A).

**Sheet structure** (43 columns):
- Cols A-G: Family, Transaction Type, Doc No, Date, Party From, Party To, Remarks
- Cols H-AR: 34 survey columns with ✅ for surveys affected by that transaction
- Each transaction = one row
- Chronological order from UDR → current

**CRITICAL FORMAT RULES**:
- Transaction flow must go from oldest (UDR/pre-1980) → newest (current owner)
- Each row shows which specific surveys the transaction affects via ✅
- Include ALL: UDR records, partition deeds, sale deeds, settlement deeds, agreements, cancellations, death/devolvement, mutation, patta errors
- Mark ⚠️ for issues (missing DC/LHC, extent discrepancies, patta errors)
- Cross-reference Drive links from `PART_I_DocFurnished` sheet (column J)
- Use column K for Link Status ("✅", "📄 No separate file", "⚠️")

### 4. Build Flow Chart (FLOW_CHARTS sheet)
Create a tree-diagram using box-drawing chars (├── └── │) per survey series.

**Format**: 5 columns
- Col A: Tree structure with ├── └── │ ┌── prefixes
- Col B: Patta number chain (e.g., "Patta 357→1922")
- Col C: Party name chain
- Col D: Status (✅ ACQUIRED / ✅ DRA REALTY / ❌ NOT DRA / ⚠️)
- Col E: Date or doc number

**CRITICAL**: NEVER use `+` at the start of a cell — Google Sheets interprets it as a formula. Use `├──` instead. Use `valueInputOption='RAW'` when writing to avoid formula interpretation.

**Include in each chart**:
- Parent survey → bifurcation → child surveys
- Patta numbers at each stage (e.g., Patta 357→1922)
- Family/party names for each link in chain
- Acquisition status at end of chain
- ⚠️ flags for errors/issues

### 5. Cross-Reference External Index
If an existing index spreadsheet (e.g., "Ranka Oasis Saveganapalli - Legal Documents Index") has additional docs mapped to survey numbers:
- Parse column A for survey mappings (comma-separated)
- Add missing docs to each survey-wise sheet (deduplicate by Drive link)
- Mark as "✅ Added from Index"

## Pitfalls
- ✅ vs ❌ vs ⚠️: Use consistently for readability
- Party names: Keep full names from TSR (with family relations e.g., "Prema w/o Nagaraju")
- Doc numbers: Include year suffix (e.g., "21201/2023") — makes cross-referencing possible
- For rows with multiple parties, use "→" arrow for transfer direction
- In FLOW_CHARTS, indent levels show bifurcation depth (4-space indent per level)
- Always add a LEGEND row at the bottom of FLOW_CHARTS

